Remembrance of the only clergyman of the Church of England who, during the First World War, was honored as a Veterandant of the Victoria Cross, was honored 100 years later in his/her hometown.
Lt. Lt. Lt. Col. Bernard Vann was decorated on September 29, 1918 for his invading Bellenglise and Lehaucourt.
