He also said he'd become a parent made him care less about winning the Olympics.
The usual host of this multi-expanded program, Kirsty Young, has taken a few months off because of the disease.
Appearing on a show first led by Laverne, Daley said growing up, he felt “less valuable” than the others because “simultaneous liking boys and girls wasn’t social-acceptable.”
“Until now, this feeling of lesser value and being different is something that gives me the strength to be successful.”
He said that he wished to prove that he was “worth something” not to disappoint everyone when they finally find out about his sexuality.
A two-time Olympic bronze medalist has become a high-profile activist of the LGBT community and used his performance at this year’s Commonwealth Games in Australia to call on more countries to decriminalize homosexuality.
